# Figma slots (design ↔ code)

Source framing: [The Case for Slots](https://southleft.substack.com/p/the-case-for-slots) (TJ / Southleft).
Figma docs: [Use slots](https://help.figma.com/hc/en-us/articles/19708407034007) ·
[Slots vs swaps vs variants](https://help.figma.com/hc/en-us/articles/19708410785559).

## Mental model

| Mechanism | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| **Variant** | Finite states you enumerate ahead of time |
| **Instance swap** | Replace one *known* component with another *known* one from a list |
| **Slot** | A named hole + **contract** for content you don’t know yet (including content that doesn’t exist today) |

Slots are not “fancy swaps.” Swaps pick from a menu; slots define *how* content must behave while leaving *what* open.

## Where it matters

Prefer slots for **layout infrastructure** (grid, feature section, card shell, section header, media/actions rows) — not only for leaf controls (Button, Badge).

Before slots, reusable layouts meant variant explosion or detach-and-rebuild. With slots: structure once, content flows into named areas, layout holds.

## Nesting (“slot inception”)

Figma does **not** nest a slot node inside a slot node. You **can** place a **slot-enabled component instance** inside another slot. Layers stay editable and linked to sources — no detach required.

Typical stack: layout slot → card (with its own slots) → button group / media / actions.

## Code mapping (Fabely)

When reading Figma or authoring composition:

- Named slots ↔ React `children` / named subcomponents (`ItemMedia`, `ItemActions`, `CardHeader`, …) — **open content, fixed chrome**
- Axes that must stay enumerable (size, tone, state) stay **variants / props**
- Prefer “contract + composition” over prop matrices that anticipate every future combination
- In Storybook, demonstrate the **slot contract** (what may go in each hole), not only one fixed demo tree

## Do / don’t

- **Do** treat layout shells as first-class components with open content areas
- **Do** keep slot contracts tight (alignment, gap, max lines) even when content is open
- **Don’t** encode open content as endless variants or required instance-swap menus
- **Don’t** detach layout instances to “just change the middle”

